/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:401:* ''Step 2, the key's seat'': a content key's lockbox, the store that rests lockboxes, records and the chunk index, and the content-key holder stand as law at <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/sealed-store#/the-store">>, and that carrier names each part the code holds. A node vessel's daemon island seats the holder beside its Keyhive identities and subscribes the content-key roll to its own seat rolls; a removal's successor wraps for the readers that remain, each lockbox into a Keyhive document of its own, so a removed device opens nothing a vessel seals after it counts the raise. Owed from this step, each to its owner: the session open that hands the island a signer and the chain check, without which no content key mints on a production vessel; a door from the island to the vessel's fold for the raises it counts; the face join's call for a from-now admission or a hand-over; and the browser shore's rest and Archive writer. A raise over the vessel that founded a face's key group names no seat a roll can leave out, so that vessel keeps its keys until `K12` stands a fresh group. What steps three and four take from this step reads at <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/sealed-store#/owed">>.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:450:* ''Integrity owed: face isolation, end to end'' (`K15` step 3, `B1`; `F6`'s slice three rides here with Wave B). Its witness: one adversarial multi-tab, multi-face run in a real browser, an unadmitted port, a stale generation, a cross-face sealed write and the last session's lock, where today only fake islands read them. MEASURED (the fresh read of Wave B; the readers, 2026-10-20). Wave B (PR #81) builds the guards and their reds on fake islands and the node; the real-browser adversarial run waits on Wave C's one SharedWorker per house.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:451:* ''Integrity owed: identity authority enforced, beyond the prose'' (`K15` step 6). Its witness: Wave C's red suite, a forged selector and a coherent foreign bundle refused, one sequence signed twice surfacing as a fork, a frontier that never falls. LEAD on the suite's shape; MEASURED that today's gate verifies continuity alone (`boot-daemon-keyhive.ts`).
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:459:* `K15` One hive per face (#/rulings, 2026-10-18): each PersonaGroup owns its Keyhive identity, event store, registry, archive and content-key seat, and no identity stands above them. Build order, each step red-first: (0) before bytes move, the custody contract of <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-custody-step-zero">>: the node and browser row census sorted D, F or S, the FCK key class, each face's own slot tree and recovery route, the carrier binding of face, row name and kind, and the overwrite contract generalized to a row-class key (#/rulings, a face's custody rows seal under its own key; a shared act never makes a shared secret) (the node census built, PR #70: each carrier row names its target classes, a LEAD mark and its open joint, and `encodeCarrierContext` spells the D and S seal context; the archive-row-selector joint traced and held open, PR #71: no archive site hands its row an authenticated PersonaGroup); (1) a substrate probe that two Keyhive instances in one process hold apart under interleaved acts, a reboot and a cross-read (measured: isolation holds, `packages/lararium-keyhive/tests/two-hives-one-process.probe.test.ts`), then a face context with its own store, registry, archive and key seat; (2) the face as the sole owner of its identity and group, the vessel's delegation gone from every face-bearing event (built, PR #68: `makeFaceBagDoor`, `faceOwnerVerifier`, a two-face event-byte capture its red, `W25`'s probe its regression), and 2b, a bag keeping one Document across boots (built, PR #68: `registerBagsDurably`, its record on the daemon doc for the vessel's ground and on each face's plane for that face's bags); the door grants the face's group before it records a Document (PR #69), so a crash between them re-enters to the same end; (2c, operator ruling 2026-10-19; built, PR #79) the atom cut: a random atom per (vessel, PersonaGroup) under that face's FCK signs every act on the face's behalf on node and browser, the place signer keeps the floor's duties alone, the wire subjects and verifiers move together, and its genesis, admit and founding-bootstrap deltas ride `X0` by `genesis/unbaked.json`, red-first on a thief holding the place seed deriving no veil and opening no group secret; on the local presence channel the session wears the mounted face, so a verb's presenter derives from the island's own atom and never from the CLI's unsigned `requestedBy`, the floor presents the place for floor acts alone, and a verb that names another face refuses by name (#/rulings, a session wears the face, 2026-10-11; a published atom key would link face and vessel on a wire); (3) sessions and registries routed by one face, no union, with `F6` slice three's asker-seals beside it, each sealer holding its row class's key (built, PR #81: the browser house keys by (PersonaGroup, persona root), the island proves each face through `gate:clear` while the holder holds no key, the island reads the fleet board's dyad itself, a fresh group mints a fresh atom, founding seeds key by their ask digest, and the node keys its atom and veil-archive rows by PersonaGroup digest; the daemon's last unions ride step 6); (4) content keys and removal per face, `K12`'s fresh group inside it; (5) a one-face restore and a herm that carries yet authors nothing; (6) the fence migration, identity bytes, split stores, slot trees and FCKs, and archive and custody formats together, under one identity model (#/rulings, sync carries, verification decides: the sealed anchor, the signed `@persona` log, verified projections): each D row (the atom's seed, its archive) seals under its face's FCK, where the node now seals them under the seated vessel key, and keys by its PersonaGroup, as the node's atom and veil-archive rows and the browser's atom row already do, where the browser's veil archive still keys by handle index. The isolation red: unlock face A alone, bypass every route, and try to open and replace B's occupied carriers with every key A holds, the S key included; each open fails, B's bytes stand unchanged, and A's bundle restored on a fresh vessel holds nothing of B. Lead: DreamNet-Wright after `W26`'s floor slice lands. K, W. Wave C (step 6 under the identity anchor, `readFace` as the one door with its census) landed in PR #86 on 2026-10-23. `K15-H` (the Handle owner rides the anchor, the row in `docs/pono/k15-wave-c-lane`) landed in PR #88. Wave D (the FCK fence, its eight slices whole, kit `docs/pono/k15-wave-d-lane`) landed in PR #95 on 2026-10-26: each face seals its D rows under its own FCK, unlocks apart, bundles and restores alone, lifts its anon veil on join, and seats when its grant arrives. `K17`'s realm leg (`docs/pono/k17-realm-lease-lane`) landed in PR #97 on 2026-10-26.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:460:* `B1` Browser custody. The custody API stands specified in `browser-custody.ts`: a passphrase or paper (2-of-3) slot binds the slot tree, the device seed and every Keyhive Archive move into sealed carriers through the mesh's one sealed writer, a wrong route refuses and changes no byte, a locked keystore refuses `sealed-locked` before any mint, and the clear-password act asks through the confirm door and answers only to a literal yes. The boot stands (PRs #48 and #61): the vessel lock gives back on a throw and a `sealed-locked` boot retries in the same page, the web boot asks the unlock through its own form, the clear verb answers `asks` and calls no door before a literal yes, the wiki's `tm-clear-password` road asks through TW5's confirm road and writes no synced tiddler, the question names what it clears, and a declined unlock retries in the page. Under #/rulings (a shared act never makes a shared secret) the browser holds no vessel key, so the clear names one face and clears that face's rows, built inside `K15` steps 0 through 3. Owed: the persona roots, which still rest in the clear outside the tree, sealed under it, with the mint refusing until a slot binds (#/rulings); the browser's vessel-key rotation; and the passkey slot, after its derivation gets measured (`B3`) and never alone. Each tab asks for its own unlock, and the ask admits that tab to its face's open hive while the holder keeps a face's keys only while some session of that face stands unlocked (#/rulings, 2026-10-18; the research and its leads at <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/research/session-unlock-2026">>). Built with `K15` step 3 (PR #81): the holder answers a port only for a session it admitted, an unadmitted port asking for a sealed body refusing by name, and the last session of a face to close locks that face's hive; the production holder lifecycle stays a named skip on every engine until Wave C's one SharedWorker per house. B.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:468:* `K12` A fresh PersonaGroup for a seat no hand can revoke (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/kapae#/keys">>). The PersonaGroup stands as a Keyhive group, so every other seat's revocation rolls the bags the group reaches (`persona-group-roll`); revoke authority follows the seating lineage, so a seat whose seating hand left, and the founder's own seat, leave only by a fresh group. Owed first: a name the face keeps across groups, since its plane names key on the group's id. It builds inside `K15`'s per-face removal step. K.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:483:* `K16` The Teshima Family Council (#/rulings, 2026-10-18; <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cabal-realm">>), `K15`'s acceptance story. Kalani founds a private council; Leilani joins it with two of her three faces. Red-first, after `K15`'s face context: (1) the council's hive as a Keyhive group holding no key of its own, its members the chosen faces' own identities; (2) an invite walks Leilani to the door, the threshold grafts each chosen face, a face leaves by its own act, and another's removal rides `kapae` or a fork by omission; (3) a member face's photo lands in its working layer of the council wiki and reaches the council's canon by `MOVE` (`W27`); (4) both chosen faces read it, the face kept back reads nothing and learns nothing, and no event in the council's history names a creator or issuer that ties two of Leilani's faces together; (5) a herm carries the sealed book and authors nothing (`K15` step 5). The e2e set stands four vessels: Kalani's, one per chosen face of Leilani's, and a herm. The e2e set walks the council at one hearth first: Kalani's seed charter holds the realm and Leilani's chosen faces walk there as guests, no Nexus founded (#/rulings, one charter). The two-hearth council follows, under the Nexus the two found, and there the member consult that lets a realm's documents cross between two operators reads a root map nothing fills (cabal-realm #/many-realms, owed), and the climb from seed charter to Nexus re-pins the realm by a named act (owed). Open joints: a quorum Handle with a seated key stands only where the council signs as one name, and that key signs collective acts alone, reaching no member's hive (#/the-steward-signer, owed). K, W.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:490:* `E2` The serving key's custody and its unattended road (#/rulings, the ember's key at rest; <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/custody#/the-table">>). Built: the fifth class `serving` in the carrier table, read by the census and `vault status`; SK minted at the founding; `sk-slots` with the vessel key's entry, opened at every human unlock and re-wrapped by a vessel-key rotation. Owed: the serving rows under SK and SK's own rotation; no minting secret in any serving row; the anchor path, where an ember slot answers unattended only against a hardware-sealed hearth key whose attestation the ember checks on each ask; the confirm path, where every slot of a hearth with no such anchor answers only on a person's confirm and threshold two asks a second confirm, never an unattended raise; and the bare deny-only `sk-rotation-owed` mark that any counted removal sets and that refuses every ask until SK rolls (`vault-carriers.ts`, `keyslot.ts`, `custody-seat.ts`). E.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:524:* `W28` The sealed channel's frame layout stands frozen (`gate-exchange.ts` `GATE_FRAME`; kit <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/w28-gate-lane">> #/the-frozen-frames): six tags in two direction blocks, a reserved-tag rule so a later frame adds a tag and moves none, fixed body and subject bounds and 65-byte finish and verdict frames, witnessed by `gate-frame-freeze.test.ts`. The gate answers an upgrade only after its first flight decrypts (`FaceGate.preflight`), so a flight no bundle opens draws a destroyed socket before any 101. No wire byte moved. Built, PR #96. W.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:525:* `W29` The place signs by a scoped signer under a pre-rotated KEL (#/rulings, the place signs by a scoped signer, 2026-10-19; kit <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/w29-place-kel-lane">>): built, PR #98, 2026-10-26. One KEL grammar (`vessel-kel.ts`, beside `persona-kel` and `handle-kel`): the inception seats the online signer and commits a cold next-key digest; a rotation reveals that key, which signs it, seats a replacement signer and commits a fresh next key; no interaction events. Every founding door, node, hearth, herm kindle and browser alike, mints the armed inception and lands no byte before the founding card reads back through the `PlaceFoundingCard` port, and the cold seed rests on no file. `lares vessel rotate` runs the card ceremony: it verifies the old card against the head, reads the replacement card back, then stages, publishes and reconciles under one custody claim, and a restart never invents a successor. Peers learn the head from the Nexus carriage board and an offline herm from the carry bundle; one fold, bounded at 64 rows and 8 pieces of fork evidence per AID, refuses a gap, a rollback and a fork. The five floor duties sign and verify `len(D) ‖ D ‖ preimage`. A seed census names every raw-seed consumer and fails on a new one. Owed: a browser ceremony UI that seats a card (until it lands, the browser's KEL door refuses by name and a browser leaf holds no place KEL); the duty verifiers resolving their signer at the head (`verifyPlaceDutyAtHead`), with `W14`–`W16`; the seed's other reach, K15's bonds, named in the census. W.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:537:* ''Integrity owed: the bake's cross-product'' (`X0`, touching `K15` step 6, `W26`, `G37`). Its witness: one matrix over the pre-bake and post-bake artifacts, every old CID refused after the bake and a fresh two-of-two founding standing, rather than greens read row by row.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:545:* `X0` The founding bake: one deliberate re-genesis before a second operator stands, after which CIDs are meant to last because another operator pins them. It moves together `K15` step 6 (identity bytes, split stores, slot trees and FCKs, archive and custody formats, each face's random device veil), the place KEL's pre-rotation and the scoped place signer (the signer frames each duty's domain itself, signing `len(D) ‖ D ‖ preimage` and its verifiers the same, so no signed floor image carries its own separation; built with `W29`, whose readiness red reads a fresh genesis founded armed, the five framed pairs verifying, and an old-shape inception refused by name, `old-shape-inception`), `W26`'s closing bake (the floor release), and `G37`'s preimage and format renames (`engine/v1` and its kin, the floor announcement's kind, the genesis seed and CAS formats). Each member carries its own readiness red, so the bake waits on the slowest by name, never on a date; the bake's own red: a fresh genesis founds, no CID from before the bake verifies after it, and a mixed old archive refuses by name. The gate it opens: a second operator may found a Nexus fresh at two of two. X.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:576:* `K13` The sealed outbox (#/rulings; <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/custody#/the-table">>). Parcels rest sealed under random names in the `outbox` class. Owed: carriage shipping, idempotent receipt and local delete after ship. K.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:594:* `F6` The browser holder as owner, with unicast replies. Slice one stands (PR #56): a closed routing table (`holder-routes.ts`) sends each island message to exactly one port, a reply by its request id, camera traffic by its lease, the island's own asks to its owner port, and drops a kind with no route by name. Slice two stands (PR #58): every tab-to-holder message rides a random owner epoch, a session and a generation, and the holder refuses a stale or unknown one by name to that port alone; `session:open` with its face waits on `W4`'s face supplier. Slices three and four move the Repo and the daemon kernel into the holder; their sealed writes go to the asker (#/rulings, the asker seals). Slice three stands with `K15` step 3 (PR #81): the holder routes each sealed write to the session that caused it, and Chromium, which exposes no nested Worker inside a SharedWorker, takes the dedicated-worker floor, its swap waiting for the worker's `ready` before it replays the manifest and retiring the crossing it replaces. Slice four stays owed. O1.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:596:* `F9` The switch; the vessel-wide selector retires. Its one persisted shape, the selector's two stores (the node's active-persona index and the browser's `ACTIVE_PERSONA_STORE`), retired with `K15` Wave D (PR #95): the worn face lives as session state on node and browser, and no store keeps it. The switch act itself lands additive. O1.
